<h3>Lead Response Time: The Hidden Conversion Killer</h3>
<p>Response time is the single biggest lever for improving conversion — and it costs nothing.</p>
<ul>
<li>Responding within 60 seconds increases conversion by 391%</li>
<li>Waiting 5+ minutes loses 80% of qualifying odds</li>
<li>Half of electrical service traffic comes after hours</li>
</ul>
<p>Implement:<br />
- <strong>Auto-reply texts</strong>: Immediate acknowledgment when someone fills out a form<br />
- <strong>24/7 answering service</strong>: Live answer for after-hours emergency calls<br />
- <strong>AI chatbots</strong>: Qualify leads and schedule appointments 24/7<br />
- <strong>Call routing</strong>: Direct emergency calls to on-call technicians</p>
<h3>Seasonal Performance Analysis</h3>
<p>Track leads and revenue by month and by service type. Identify patterns:<br />
- Which months generate the most emergency calls?<br />
- Which services spike before storm season?<br />
- What is your commercial pipeline 3, 6, and 12 months out?<br />
- Which marketing channels perform best in each season?</p>
<p>Use this data to allocate budget dynamically. Shift spend from underperforming channels to high-performing ones. Pre-position campaigns before predictable demand surges.</p>
<h3>The 90-Day Review Cycle</h3>
<p>Every 90 days, conduct a marketing performance review:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Revenue attribution</strong>: Which channels generated revenue this quarter?</li>
<li><strong>Cost per booked job</strong>: Are you paying more or less than last quarter?</li>
<li><strong>Close rate trends</strong>: Is your sales process improving or declining?</li>
<li><strong>Customer acquisition cost</strong>: What percentage of job value goes to marketing?</li>
<li><strong>Lifetime value</strong>: Are you attracting one-time customers or repeat clients?</li>
<li><strong>Market mix</strong>: Is your residential/commercial split where you want it?</li>
</ol>
<p>Adjust strategy based on findings. Double down on what works. Cut what does not.</p>
