<h2>Conclusion: Your 90-Day Electrical Marketing Action Plan</h2>
<p>Electrical contractor marketing is not about doing everything. It is about doing the right things for the right market at the right time.</p>
<p>The dual-market framework gives you clarity: residential marketing is about being findable and trustworthy in the moment of need. Commercial marketing is about building relationships that lead to invitations. EV charger and generator marketing are about capturing the fastest-growing segments before your competitors do.</p>
<h3>Key Takeaways</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Segment your marketing</strong>: Residential and commercial buyers need different messages, channels, and follow-up systems</li>
<li><strong>Own local search</strong>: Your Google Business Profile is your most valuable marketing asset for residential leads</li>
<li><strong>Build commercial relationships</strong>: General contractors and property managers are your path to six-figure projects</li>
<li><strong>Capture EV and generator demand</strong>: These are the highest-growth service lines in electrical contracting</li>
<li><strong>Track everything</strong>: Cost per booked job, not cost per click, is the metric that matters</li>
<li><strong>Respond fast</strong>: A 60-second response time increases conversion by 391% — and it is free</li>
</ul>
<h3>Your Next Steps</h3>
<p><strong>Week 1-2: Foundation</strong><br />
- Audit your Google Business Profile and optimize for emergency services<br />
- Create separate residential and commercial paths on your website homepage<br />
- Implement automated review requests</p>
<p><strong>Week 3-4: Content and SEO</strong><br />
- Publish dedicated pages for EV charger installation and generator installation<br />
- Create location-specific pages for your top 5 service areas<br />
- Start a "When to Call an Electrician" content series</p>
<p><strong>Week 5-8: Paid Advertising</strong><br />
- Launch Google Ads with separate emergency and service campaigns<br />
- Set up Google Local Services Ads<br />
- Create LinkedIn company page and begin posting commercial case studies</p>
<p><strong>Week 9-12: Systems and Tracking</strong><br />
- Implement call tracking with source attribution<br />
- Build email automation sequences for quotes, reviews, and maintenance reminders<br />
- Establish 90-day review cycle</p>
<p>The electrical contractors who win in 2026 will not be the ones with the biggest marketing budget. They will be the ones with the clearest understanding of their two markets — and the systems to serve both.</p>
